## `.gitignore`

This covers:
- Python virtualenv + caches
- environment files
- OS/IDE junk
- (optional) Next.js build folders if you ever store frontend + backend in one repo

```gitignore
# ---------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.so
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
env/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------
# Environment / secrets
# ---------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example